# Template Skill

Rename this folder to your skill's name, make the `name:` in the frontmatter match
the folder exactly, then rewrite everything below.

## How to use this skill

State when the agent should apply it: reactively after work is produced, live while
writing, or on explicit request. Be concrete about the trigger.

## Adapt to the project first

Before applying any rule, read the surrounding code and match its conventions.
Project convention beats the generic rule in this file.

## Rules

Keep rules numbered, specific, and checkable. Each one should say what to do, what
the failure looks like, and why it matters.

1. **Rule name.** What to do. What the violation looks like in practice.
2. **Rule name.** ...

## Self-check before delivery

- [ ] Every rule above was applied to the changed files, not just skimmed.
- [ ] Anything deliberately skipped is called out with a reason.
- [ ] Claims about behaviour were verified against the code, not recalled.

## References

Put deep material in `references/*.md` and link it here. Those files load only when
the agent needs them, which keeps this entrypoint cheap:

- [references/example.md](references/example.md) — when to read it.
